Extending a class allows us to modify the behaviour of inherited public or protected methods.
This is called overriding.

The procedure is simple: we Re-implement the method using the same signature, return values and parameters.
Sometimes we want to access the parent method and add a few improvements of our own in this case we use the word
super - this keyword gives us access to our parent-class
super.method() calls the super class implementation in a ctr it calls the super class ctr.

you can call an empty super() only if the parent has an empty ctr, else it will generate a compiler error
however there will always be a call of the sub class to the super class ctr default so if the super class has no default one.
you will get an error when calling the ctr of public B
